<h1>Quality management</h1>

<p>Quality at Meridian Castings is managed under a single group system that covers all three sites, overseen by our Director of Quality, Susan Ogden. The system is built around ISO 9001:2015, with the Sheffield and Wrexham sites also holding IATF 16949:2016 for automotive customers and AS9100D for aerospace-related work.</p>

<p>Incoming raw materials are checked against certified mill and cast records before release to production. In-process checks include coordinate measuring, dye penetrant and magnetic particle inspection, and radiographic inspection for castings carrying internal soundness requirements. Final inspection records are retained against the part's heat and batch numbers for a minimum of ten years.</p>

<p>Customer complaints are logged and investigated through a formal corrective-action process, with root cause and containment actions reported back to the customer within agreed timescales. Repeat issues are reviewed at a monthly quality meeting attended by representatives from all three sites.</p>

<p>Full details of our certificates are listed on the <a href="/certifications">certifications</a> page. Our approach to environmental management, including waste sand reclamation, is covered under <a href="/sustainability">sustainability</a>.</p>
